Q3. Memory Bottleneck Debugging
Answer
Memory Map
Code  : 5 MB

Heap  : 150 MB

Stack : 1 MB × 25 Threads = 25 MB

Total Memory Used = 180 MB

Physical RAM Available = 2 GB
Debug Analysis
Although the system has 2 GB of RAM, the multi-threaded program experiences frequent page faults.
The large heap (150 MB) and 25 threads accessing memory simultaneously reduce memory locality.
As a result, the operating system frequently loads required pages from disk into RAM, causing page faults and slowing execution.
Root Cause
Large Heap Usage
        +
Multiple Threads
        +
Poor Memory Locality
        ↓
Frequent Page Faults
        ↓
Performance Degradation
Optimizations
1. Reduce Heap Memory Usage
Free unused memory.
Reuse allocated memory.
Use memory pools to reduce unnecessary allocations.
2. Optimize Thread Usage
Use a thread pool instead of creating many threads.
Reduce stack size per thread if possible.
Result
Page Faults Reduced

Memory Usage Optimized

Execution Speed Improved

Overall Performance Increased
